on 62% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 79% of field goals, which is a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into receivers, about 19% of the money on the books. Their linebackers were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Dak Prescott has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,046 yards. CeeDee Lamb has been the clear top target with 31% of the looks and 709 receiving yards. Javonte Williams has handled most of the work in the backfield with 76% of the carries. On defense, Quinnen Williams leads the team with 5 sacks.","coaching":"Brian Schottenheimer is calling the offense as head coach and Christian Parker is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Seahawks and the 2022 Colts under Frank Reich. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Saints under Dennis Allen and the 2023 Eagles.","trends":"The offense went from 5th in EPA per play in 2025 to 7th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 32nd in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 31st so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was pre-snap motion rate, which went from 59% to 46%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}